Gary Oldman stars in Slow Horses on Apple TV.

slow horses

Spy Thriller (2022)

Creator: Will Smith

Starring: Gary Oldman, Kristin Scott Thomas

From the Apple TV platform, we choose a very special spy series from Britain, which has already released its first two seasons. According to the script, the famous MI5 has a special department, “The Pit”, where it sends agents and officers who fail miserably or make mistakes that cost the service. Presiding there is Jackson Lamb (Gary Oldman), who openly encourages his subordinates to do absolutely nothing; However, some of them disobey orders, and soon the entire department becomes embroiled in high-profile national security issues.

Drunk, foul-mouthed, sarcastic but also a terrible genius, Oldman’s character – and performance – is in itself a great reason to watch the series, which nonetheless has many other virtues. At first it was a fear of his rival, the director of MI5, who was also perfectly embodied by Kristin Scott Thomas.

Balancing thrills with suspense and an ever-terrifying mood, this ode to “losers,” losers in utterly competitive Western society, is a fresh proposition in a generally saturated genre. He also managed to touch on the real problems of the modern world, such as the resurgence of the far right, racism, inequality, etc. Without a lack of correct wooden political imagination.

Holy Spider ★★★

Thriller (2022)

Directed by: Ali Abbasi

Explanations: Amir Ebrahimi visited Mehdi Bagestani

From the Cinobo platform, we choose a very nice movie that we saw a few months ago in cinemas. Iranian Ali Abbasi uses a Danish production and shoots in Jordan, referring though exclusively to his homeland, where his film would be impossible. In the holy city of Mohsed, Iran, a serial killer stalks the streets of the night as he executes prostitutes.

The peaceful family man believes that this is how he cleanses the world from sin. Until a daring reporter arrives in town to cover the story, and ends up taking the bait to expose him.

Abbasi addresses the issue of misogyny that characterizes Iranian society, through a haunting suspense thriller, following both a female journalist heroine and a hardened killer. Indeed, the treatment of the latter by the rest of society masks the most infuriating grounds of truth.

